  "body": "**What.** From #213, take max |\u0394\u03c3_n/\u03c3_n| for n = 18\u201322 between J 1250 and J 1500 at the three nodes, and compare it with 3e-12. Recommended by the #214 agent.\n\n**Why.** #214's planted arc family reproduces the real data's spread over approximants only with about 3e-12 relative noise. #213's J differences are the direct measure of whether the \u03c3 carry errors at that level.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).**\n- If the difference is \u2265 1e-12, `second_zero.py real` is rerun with it as noise, and the crossing is reported.\n- If it is < 1e-13, the report says the spread is structural.\n- Between the two, the numbers are reported and the coordinator decides.\n\n**Depends on.** #213, #214.\n",
